.TH MD_GET_STATE 3 "2026-10-16" "libmorsedec 0.3.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_get_state \- query the current channel decoding state
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

enum morsedec_state md_get_state(const morsedec_decoder_t *decoder);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Query the current channel decoding state.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I decoder
Decoder handle. Calls using this handle must be serialized, including queries.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns an enum morsedec_state value. NULL decoder or no current channel
returns MORSEDEC_STATE_NONE. This query has no errno-based failure return.
.SH REMARKS
MORSEDEC_STATE_NONE means no selected channel. MORSEDEC_STATE_PAUSE and
MORSEDEC_STATE_DECODING identify an automatically selected channel;
MORSEDEC_STATE_LOCKED_PAUSE and MORSEDEC_STATE_LOCKED_DECODING identify a
pinned one. DECODING describes the channel decoder state, not the
instantaneous key-up/key-down observation. A PAUSE state can still have
message history. Use md_get_channel() to inspect each tracked channel rather
than only the selected channel.
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Serialize all calls that access the same handle, including getters. Different
handles may process concurrently after construction. These functions are not
specified as async-signal-safe.
.SH VERSION
This md_ entry point is available since libmorsedec 0.2.0.
Version 0.3.0 uses the float API and shared-library ABI 2.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmorsedec (3),
.BR md_get_channel (3),
.BR md_get_frequency (3),
.BR md_pin_frequency (3)
